<%# The "You May Also Like" section. The build renders it from the order that the api calculates
    from the article text, the links, and the concepts (data/related.json, through
    `rake import:related`). It renders nothing when the entry has no neighbor, and that is what
    removed the widget that this section replaced.

    related_section removes the two adjacent entries, which read_next renders on this same page.
    scope_entry_ids stays necessary: the two sections can still name one entry when the api list
    changes between two builds. `article` is a necessary local. %>
<% related = related_section(article) %>
<% if related.present? %>
  <%= partial 'partials/collection', locals: { title: "You May Also Like", items: related, variant: "halves", scope_entry_ids: true } %>
<% end %>
